    "text": "To determine the number of students Beth had in her class at the end of her final year, we need to follow the changes in the student population step by step.\n\n1. **Initial number of students:**\n   Beth started with 150 students in her 10th-grade class.\n\n2. **Students joining the following year:**\n   The following year, 30 more students joined the class. So, we add 30 to the initial number of students:\n   \\[\n   150 + 30 = 180\n   \\]\n   Now, Beth has 180 students.\n\n3. **Students leaving in the final year:**\n   In her final year, 15 students left the class. So, we subtract 15 from the current number of students:\n   \\[\n   180 - 15 = 165\n   \\]\n   Now, Beth has 165 students.\n\nTherefore, the number of students Beth had in her class at the end of her final year is \\(\\boxed{165}\\).",
